    "narrative": "For our September 14th slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 80.88 projection. Despite facing Sandy Alcantara, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, making him our highest-floor play. **Mickey Moniak** is our secondary anchor at 73.93; his aggressive +14% park and platoon boosts against Casey Mize make him a high-leverage start, even hitting seventh. We are also capitalizing on the soft matchup against Corbin Burnes (7.87 xERA) by rolling with **Griffin Conine**, whose xwOBA of 0.371 and favorable order positioning drive his strong 60.91 score, provided the lineup holds as projected. \n\nThe optimization process was tight regarding our middle-infield depth. **Travis Bazzana** narrowly missed the cut with a 39.19 score; his platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter effectively kept him below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor,\" as the risk of a sub-optimal plate appearance outweighed the potential for a marginal gain. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** (48.52) remains in the lineup primarily for his SB utility, though his score is hampered by a significant platoon penalty. We are monitoring the status of **Moises Ballesteros**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Griffin Conine** closely; as these are \"Lineup Pending\" designations, any drop in batting order will force a re-evaluation of their projected efficiency against their respective starters. **Gabriel Moreno** rounds out a solid core, leveraging a strong order position (#3) to maximize his opportunities against Alcantara.",
